# CREDITS — The Open Top

A 40-second film in the Whiteboard Explainer style, made entirely in code.
The mug, the heat, and the lesson are invented. No brand is shown.

## Voice
Speech synthesis: Kokoro (kokoro-onnx), voice `af_heart`, English (`en-us`).
Model and engine: https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx
Offline synthesis. The voice model is fetched by the FilmCode library's voice tier.

## Music
Original score for this film (`music/score.py`).
Kalimba and nylon guitar are physically modelled (`core/audio/pluck.py`), not sampled.
No sample library is used.

## Sound effects
All foley is synthesised for this film (`mix.py`): room tone, wall-clock ticks,
marker strokes, eraser, magnet clicks, cap.

## Typefaces
- Cormorant Garamond (upright and italic) — SIL Open Font License 1.1,
  Catharsis Fonts. See `fonts/OFL.txt`.
  Used for the burned subtitles. Board lettering is drawn as single strokes
  by the film, not set from a font file.

## Picture
Every frame is drawn by this film's marker engine (`engine/wb.js`).
No stock footage, no photographs, no third-party images.
